---- SYNCHRONIZATION ----

>> A3: Explain how your code avoids a race if two processes attempt to
>> extend a file at the same time.

To prevent a race if two processes attempt to extend a file at the 
same time, we implemented an inode-level lock (every inode has a 
lock), 'inode_lock'. 

Extending files occurs in inode_write_at when offset + size 
exceeds the current file length. If this criteria is met,
the current thread acquires the lock and any other thread
trying to extend the file must wait before the current 
thread releases the lock.

