---- SYNCHRONIZATION ----

>> B4: How do you prevent races on directory entries?  For example,
>> only one of two simultaneous attempts to remove a single file
>> should succeed, as should only one of two simultaneous attempts to
>> create a file with the same name, and so on.

Before performing any directory operations, the current thread 
acquires the directory's inode_lock. This prevents all possible 
race conditions. For example, when two threads try to create a 
file with the same name simultaneously, both will call dir_add.
The first one to acquire the inode lock scans the directory, 
finds the name free, inserts the new entry, and releases the 
lock. The second thread then acquires the lock, sees
the name already exists, and fails.

